# AUTHOR LINE GROUPING — the SINGLE-ROW cell, and it is a NEGATIVE.
#
# MUST EXCLUDE from any bulk `gg fmt` sweep: this fixture is a deliberately
# UNFORMATTED INPUT — the assertion is on what `gg fmt` turns it INTO
# (`fmt_author_rows_single_row_is_not_a_grouping`, exact text). A sweep would
# rewrite it into its own expected output and the cell would go green-vacuous.
#
# AXIS = grouping shape, SINGLE-ROW cell: the container spans several lines, but
# every element sits on ONE of them, so the author expressed no break BETWEEN
# elements and there is no grouping to preserve. The ENGAGEMENT GUARD leaves the
# list at the ratified one-element-per-line magic-comma shape.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE CELL THE GUARD EXISTS FOR. Without it, `[\n 1, 2, y,\n]` comes
# back as a half-exploded one-row list nobody asked for; measured, three corpus
# fixtures change and `fmt_magic_comma_author_paren_cells_spaced` reds.
#
# NO PRE-FIX RED IS POSSIBLE — the pre-change binary emits exactly the expected
# text, because this is the behaviour the guard PRESERVES rather than one it
# adds. RED-verified the other way (Core #12), by BREAKING the mechanism: with
# the engagement guard removed from
# `Formatter::format_bracketed_broken_with_comments`, the output becomes the
# author's own one-row shape and the exact-text assertion reds. Restored after
# measuring.
from std.collections import Vector

void main():
    int y = 3
    Vector[int] xs = [
        1, 2, y,
    ]
    print(xs.len())
